1. printf (C library, buffered)
2. write() (thin C library wrapper)
3. syscall(SYS_write, ...) (number chosen by hand)
SYS_write is number 1, SYS_getpid is number 39 on this machine
getpid() equals syscall(SYS_getpid): yes
write with a bad pointer returned -1, errno 14 (Bad address)
system call 99999 returned -1, errno 38 (Function not implemented)
